1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Small eateries buy
ingredients before anyone orders.

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,719
Too much and food is wasted;

3
00:00:05,769 --> 00:00:07,955
too little and customers leave.

4
00:00:08,005 --> 00:00:09,325
BunnBaa fixes that:

5
00:00:09,375 --> 00:00:14,950
diners pay ahead to lock a meal, and the
earlier they lock, the cheaper it is.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,282
Onboarding takes one photo.

7
00:00:19,332 --> 00:00:29,870
Gemini's vision model reads the menu
and drafts every item — name,

8
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:37,570
English name, price,
dietary tags and allergens.

9
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:44,950
Nothing goes live until
the owner confirms it.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,538
Diners don't have to browse ten shops.

11
00:00:50,588 --> 00:00:52,597
They just ask.

12
00:00:52,647 --> 00:01:02,450
Gemini calls our server-side tools to
check menus, availability and

13
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:10,244
meal plans, and returns meals
they can actually book.

14
00:01:10,294 --> 00:01:12,009
It suggests;

15
00:01:12,059 --> 00:01:14,068
it never buys.

16
00:01:14,118 --> 00:01:19,950
Booking two days ahead saves 20 percent.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,408
Plans change.

18
00:01:21,458 --> 00:01:28,027
Instead of wasting the meal, the
diner lists it for resale.

19
00:01:28,077 --> 00:01:34,421
Gemini embeddings and Firestore
vector search find people

20
00:01:34,471 --> 00:01:39,918
nearby who like similar
food, and we notify them.

21
00:01:39,968 --> 00:01:44,966
The new buyer pays, and
the original buyer is

22
00:01:45,016 --> 00:01:49,678
refunded automatically as platform points.

23
00:01:49,728 --> 00:01:54,950
That's a meal rescued — and
we count every one.

24
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,328
After the 20:00 cut-off, the
vendor has an exact count

25
00:02:01,378 --> 00:02:06,052
and a ready-made prep and purchase list.

26
00:02:06,102 --> 00:02:14,438
For the days after that, BigQuery's
TimesFM model forecasts demand, and

27
00:02:14,488 --> 00:02:21,407
k-means groups the regulars, with
Gemini naming each group.

28
00:02:21,457 --> 00:02:22,706
AI advises;

29
00:02:22,756 --> 00:02:24,950
the vendor decides.

30
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,273
At the counter, a signed
QR code is scanned.

31
00:02:30,323 --> 00:02:39,950
Any meal still unclaimed becomes a free
charity meal, so it still feeds someone.

32
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,995
Every booking streams into
BigQuery, so we can show

33
00:02:43,045 --> 00:02:45,562
meals saved and how
close the forecast was.

34
00:02:45,612 --> 00:02:47,831
BunnBaa runs entirely on Google Cloud:

35
00:02:47,881 --> 00:02:53,443
Gemini on Vertex AI, Cloud Run functions, Firestore
with vector search, BigQuery AI and Looker

36
00:02:53,493 --> 00:02:57,681
Studio — and we test the assistant with
Vertex AI's evaluation service.

37
00:02:57,731 --> 00:02:58,875
Cook what's ordered.

38
00:02:58,925 --> 00:02:59,950
Eat what's cooked.
